OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F316A1785482286
OL,3,CMan walks 6 hours down mountain after
OL,4,Cimpaling himself with hiking pole
OL,6,FTheir adventure on July 20 took a
OL,7,Fdangerous turn as Mr Cifaldi, 32,
OL,8,Fslipped and impaled himself on his own
OL,9,Fhiking pole.
OL,11,FThe 44-inch steel-tipped pole passed
OL,12,Fthrough the flesh beneath his left
OL,13,Farm, missing any vital organs, and
OL,14,Fprotruded from his back.
OL,16,FAfter assessing his wound and speaking
OL,17,Fwith his friends, Mr Cifaldi decided
OL,18,Fto walk back down the mountain due to
OL,19,Fthe high cost of a helicopter rescue.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G2/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
